    "b-sks-rc-patterns-intro": {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "props": {},
      "text": [
        {
          "insert": "PATTERN — A global table: how the original developers wrote code. A "
        },
        {
          "insert": "pattern",
          "attributes": {
            "code": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": " row is not per target; it is reusable across every target and searchable from any of them: \"which patterns match this function's opcode fingerprint?\" A row says how to spot it ("
        },
        {
          "insert": "recognizer",
          "attributes": {
            "code": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": ": an opcode-sequence fingerprint, a source shape, or a mismatch signature) and which C shape produces it ("
        },
        {
          "insert": "recipe",
          "attributes": {
            "code": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": "). The targets it was confirmed on are "
        },
        {
          "insert": "pattern_example",
          "attributes": {
            "code": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": " rows, each with the "
        },
        {
          "insert": "source",
          "attributes": {
            "code": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": " that shows it; the tactics that usually resolve it are "
        },
        {
          "insert": "pattern_tactic",
          "attributes": {
            "code": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": " rows. A target's page says a pattern applied to it through a "
        },
        {
          "insert": "target_pattern",
          "attributes": {
            "code": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": " row with a "
        },
        {
          "insert": "why",
          "attributes": {
            "code": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": ". Like "
        },
        {
          "insert": "knowledge_record",
          "attributes": {
            "code": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": " it is revisioned: a new row names the previous one in "
        },
        {
          "insert": "supersedes_id",
          "attributes": {
            "code": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": ". Standards stay a merge gate, not a table; the code graph stays a search surface, not a table."
        }
      ],
      "id": "b-sks-rc-patterns-intro",
      "children": []
    },
